            <ArticleTitle>Two-Color 810 nm STED Nanoscopy of Living Cells with Endogenous SNAP-Tagged Fusion Proteins.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acschembio.7b00616</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 810 nm STED nanoscopy setup and an appropriate combination of two fluorescent dyes (Si-rhodamine 680SiR and carbopyronine 610CP) have been developed for near-IR live-cell super-resolution imaging. Vimentin endogenously tagged using the CRISPR/Cas9 approach with the SNAP tag, together with a noncovalent tubulin label, provided reliable and cell-to-cell reproducible dual-color confocal and STED imaging of the cytoskeleton in living cells.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
